Required test cases (each is a separate top-level Test* function unless
noted):

  T1: TestBuildStateFromSignalStore_LiveValuesAlwaysWin
      Setup:
        - Live store seeded with: Odometer=99999.9, InsideTemp=21.5,
          OutsideTemp=15.0, Version="2026.4.1", BatteryLevel=80,
          VehicleSpeed=42.
        - Fake reader pre-canned to return Odometer=12345.6, InsideTemp=22.7,
          OutsideTemp=18, Version="2026.8.6" (different from live values).
      Assert:
        - state.Odometer == 99999.9 (live wins, never override).
        - state.InsideTemp == 21.5 (live wins, fresh precedence).
        - state.OutsideTemp == 15.0 (live wins).
        - state.SoftwareVersion == "2026.4.1" (live wins).
        - state.BatteryLevel == 80; state.Speed == 42.
        - fake.SnapshotAtCalls is one of {0, 1}: implementation may either
          short-circuit (no call) OR call SnapshotAt once and ignore the
          values for fields the live store already filled — both are
          acceptable; what is NOT acceptable is overriding live data with
          signal_log data.

  T2: TestBuildStateFromSignalStore_FillsZeroFieldsFromSignalLog
      Setup:
        - Live store seeded with ONLY BatteryLevel=55 and VehicleSpeed=30.
        - Fake reader returns: Odometer=12345.6, InsideTemp=22.7,
          OutsideTemp=18.0, Version="2026.8.6", IdealBatteryRange=310.0,
          RatedRange=305.0, Latitude=37.4419, Longitude=-122.1430.
      Assert (this is the headline contract):
        - state.Odometer == 12345.6
        - state.InsideTemp == 22.7
        - state.OutsideTemp == 18.0
        - state.SoftwareVersion == "2026.8.6"
        - state.IdealRange == 310.0
        - state.RatedRange == 305.0
        - state.Latitude == 37.4419
        - state.Longitude == -122.1430
        - state.BatteryLevel == 55 (live, unchanged)
        - state.Speed == 30 (live, unchanged)
        - fake.SnapshotAtCalls == 1 (signal_log was used; SnapshotAt called).
        - fake.LastVehicleID == 7 (correct vehicle).
        - fake.LastAt is within ±2s of time.Now() (point-in-time = now).

  T3: TestBuildStateFromSignalStore_MissingSignalsStayAtGoZero
      Setup:
        - Live store empty.
        - Fake reader returns map containing ONLY Odometer=42.0 (no entry
          for InsideTemp, OutsideTemp, Version, etc.).
      Assert:
        - state.Odometer == 42.0
        - state.InsideTemp == 0.0 (Go zero, no entry → stays at zero)
        - state.OutsideTemp == 0.0 (Go zero)
        - state.SoftwareVersion == "" (Go zero)
        - state.IdealRange == 0.0; state.RatedRange == 0.0
        - state.Latitude == 0.0; state.Longitude == 0.0
        - No panic, no error, no missing.*zero handling fault.

  T4: TestBuildStateFromSignalStore_SignalLogReadErrorIsTolerated
      Setup:
        - Live store seeded with Odometer=12345.0 only.
        - Fake reader pre-canned to return (nil, errors.New("snapshot at:
          read fail")). Use a sentinel error so the test can also assert it
          is NOT returned to the caller.
        - Wrap the test with a zerolog memory sink (`zerolog.New(&buf)`
          installed via `log.Logger = ...`) restored in t.Cleanup so the
          read.*fail message can be asserted to have been logged at Warn or
          Error level WITHOUT propagating; error.*log.*not propagate.
      Assert:
        - BuildStateFromSignalStore returns a non-nil *VehicleState (the
          handler must still be able to return 200 — return.*200).
        - state.Odometer == 12345.0 (live data preserved).
        - The returned value does NOT panic on access; no goroutine leak.
        - Captured log buffer contains the sentinel error message and a
          Warn/Error level — proves error is logged but not propagated.
        - The caller receives no error (the function signature has no
          error return — the contract is tolerate-and-log only).

  T5: TestBuildStateFromSignalStore_NoSignalLogReaderConfigured
